    That project declares its licence on its SourceForge page as "GNU Library or
    Lesser General Public License version 2.0 (LGPLv2)". No licence file ships in
    the release archive itself, and that label spans two distinct licences: the
    GNU Library General Public License v2.0 and the GNU Lesser General Public
    License v2.1. A copy of the LGPL v2.1 is included here as COPYING.LESSER;
    if the exact version matters for your use, confirm it with the author.

    No changes have been made to any file under libaptx100/. Files were copied
    verbatim from the upstream archive's src/libaptx100/ directory. The upstream
    release notes are preserved as UPSTREAM-readme.txt.

    Upstream notes that the plugin "uses proprietary APT-x100 codec". APT-X100 is
    a codec originally developed at Queen's University Belfast and commercialised
    by Audio Processing Technology; the foundational patents (GB8803390, filed
    1988) have long since expired.

